{
  "version": 3,
  "description": "Conformance fixture for the GraphMind loop guard, rule v3 (TS reference: packages/client/src/loop-guard.ts; binding rule: internal/decisions.md \"Loop hold v3: a loop is the same call BACK-TO-BACK\"). Ports must reproduce every `canonical` string byte for byte and every `fingerprint` (= first 32 hex chars of SHA-256 over the UTF-8 canonical string), and, for every `sequences` entry, feed the calls in order to ONE run (record the node.started, then consult the before-gate of that same call) and trip exactly at every entry of `trips` (`at` = 0-based call index whose before-gate holds, `repeats` = the count reported, `firstAt` = index of the streak's first call, i.e. what `firstSeq` points at when seq = index; `lastSeq` is always `at`); `tripsAt`/`repeatsAtTrip` repeat the first trip (null = never). Canonical form: JSON array [nodeId, input]; object keys sorted by UTF-16 code unit order (JS default sort; Python: sorted(keys, key=lambda k: k.encode(\"utf-16-be\"))); no whitespace; numbers in JS shortest round-trip form (1.0 -> 1, -0 -> 0, 1e21 -> 1e+21, NaN/Infinity -> null); strings escaped like JSON.stringify (\", \\\\, \\n, \\r, \\t, \\b, \\f, other controls < 0x20 as \\u00XX lowercase; non-ASCII kept raw); keys in `ignoreKeys` (default: only `_meta`) removed at EVERY nesting level (exact match) — pagination keys such as cursor/page/offset are NOT ignored by default; a missing input (`inputAbsent: true`) canonicalises to null. Counting (v3): per run, per node KIND, ONE streak {nodeId, fingerprint, count, firstSeq, lastSeq}. A start is WATCHED when the guard is enabled (threshold > 0, mode not off), its kind is in `kinds` (sequence field, default [\"tool\"]) and neither its nodeId nor its name is in `allowNodes` (exact match; name defaults to the nodeId after the first colon). A watched start with a readable input: same (nodeId, fingerprint) as its kind's streak -> count += 1; otherwise the streak is REPLACED by a fresh one with count 1. A watched start whose input cannot be read (`unreadable: true` — feed an input whose property read throws; also a nodeId that is not a string) CLEARS its kind's streak and has fingerprint null. Unwatched starts (other kinds, allow-listed nodes, guard off) touch no streak and have fingerprint null. The before-gate holds when its kind's streak has this nodeId, count >= threshold, and this count has not held yet (a retry with no new start does not hold again). Consequence: identical calls separated by another watched call of the same kind never trip; a model alternating two tools is not held.",
